US-012 is complete. Entity handles and worlds are implemented in a new `engine_ecs` target, and every required gate passes on the platforms I could run.

**What was built** (`engine/ecs/`)
- `EntityHandle` holds index, generation, and world id. Destroying an entity bumps its slot's generation, so a stale handle never resolves after the slot is reused. A handle from another world is rejected even when index and generation match.
- `World` is move-only and has a process-unique id. It supports `create`, `create(guid)`, `destroy`, `alive`, `find(guid)`, and `persistent_id`.
- Persistent GUIDs are stored beside the entity and are unique per world. Nil and duplicate GUIDs are rejected. GUIDs never affect indices or generations, and destroying an entity releases its GUID.

I read the PRD's Functional Requirements, Non-Goals, and Technical Considerations. The ECS sits at the path the PRD specifies, with no ready-made ECS. The benchmark contract doesn't apply yet because no harness exists, so I didn't run `engine_bench`.

**Tests** (`tests/src/ecs_world_tests.cpp`, all `[unit]`): repeated destruction, stale handles after slot reuse, 500 create/destroy cycles, 20,000-entity bulk creation with partial destruction and refill, foreign-world handles, GUID uniqueness and reuse, the same GUID in two worlds, 5,000 tagged entities, and move semantics.

**Gate results** (exit codes checked directly)
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| Linux/Clang: ValidateVendor, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug` build, `linux-unit` | Pass (0 warnings, ctest 10/10, unit suite 175 cases) |
| Linux ASan/UBSan: `linux-asan` build, `linux-sanitize` | Pass (no sanitizer reports) |
| Linux/GCC: `linux-gcc`, `linux-gcc-debug`, `linux-gcc-unit` | Pass (0 warnings, ctest 10/10) |
| Windows/MSVC 14.51: ValidateVendor, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, `win-unit` | Pass (0 `warning C`, ctest 10/10) |

Not run: GPU suites and the benchmark (no GPU backend or benchmark harness exists yet), and GitHub CI (nothing has been pushed). The `engine_tests` runner has no name filter, so I confirmed the ECS cases are in the unit suite by count and by the test object in the build, not by running them alone.

**Files changed**
- New: `engine/ecs/CMakeLists.txt`, `engine/ecs/include/engine/ecs/{entity,world}.hpp`, `engine/ecs/src/world.cpp`, `tests/src/ecs_world_tests.cpp`.
- Changed: root `CMakeLists.txt` (adds `engine/ecs`), `tests/CMakeLists.txt` (adds the test and links `engine_ecs`), `tasks/prd.json` (US-012 `passes: true`), and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` (a Codebase Patterns entry and a US-012 section).

**Choices I made**
- The handle includes a world id beyond the index and generation the story asks for. This is how a foreign-world handle is rejected.
- `World` is move-only because a copy would share the source's world id.

I did not create git commits, as the workflow asks.
